        {
          "text": "CHÊNG Man 鄭鄤 (T. 謙止, 祚長, H. 峚陽), Sept. 22, 1594–1638, Oct. 3, Ming official, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangsu. His father, Chêng Chên-hsien, 鄭振先 (T. 太初, d. Nov. 5, 1628, chin-shih of 1595), often took him when young into learned circles from which he profited greatly.",
